        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Pavel Ruminov, Terry Zwigoff, Thora Birch, Scarlett Johansson, Steve Buscemi\n- Films: Dead Daughters, Ghost World\n- Roles: film director, filmmaker, actors\n- Topics: Russian cinema, American cinema, arthouse horror, black comedy\n\nFacts:\n- Terry Zwigoff was born on May 18, 1949, and he is an American filmmaker whose work often deals with misfits, antiheroes, and themes of alienation.\n- Pavel Yurevich Ruminov was born on November 25, 1974, and he is a Russian film director.\n- Ghost World is a 2001 American black comedy film directed by Terry Zwigoff and starring Thora Birch, Scarlett Johansson, and Steve Buscemi.\n- Dead Daughters is a Russian arthouse horror film directed by Pavel Ruminov.",
